# Windows Coordinator — ignore rules
#
# Two jobs: keep build output and machine-specific state out of the repository, and make it
# impossible to commit the things that would be embarrassing or harmful (credentials, update-feed
# secrets, signing material, local paths). Anything environment-specific ships as a committed
# `.example` file with the real one ignored — see CLAUDE.md, "Never commit secrets".

# ── .NET build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `[Bb]in`/`[Oo]bj` spelled case-insensitively because MSBuild, the IDEs and hand-written scripts
# disagree about capitalisation and git is case-sensitive on Linux.
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Oo]ut/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/
artifacts/
publish/
[Pp]ublish/
TestResults/
[Tt]est[Rr]esults/
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.dSYM/
*.binlog
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json
*.nuget.props
*.nuget.targets
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
packages/
!packages/build/
.packages/
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info
*.coverage
*.coveragexml
*.opencover.xml

# ── Visual Studio ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.userprefs
*.sln.docstates
*.sln.ide/
*.vsp
*.vspx
*.psess
*.vsps
*.svclog
*.VC.db
*.VC.VC.opendb
*_i.c
*_p.c
*_h.h
*.ilk
*.meta
*.obj
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.tlb
*.tli
*.tlh
*.tmp_proj
*.log
*.tlog
*.vspscc
*.vssscc
.builds
UpgradeLog*.XML
UpgradeLog*.htm
_UpgradeReport_Files/
Backup*/

# ── JetBrains Rider / ReSharper ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
*.sln.iml
*.DotSettings.user
_ReSharper*/
*.[Rr]e[Ss]harper

# ── Visual Studio Code ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep shared, reviewable editor config; ignore per-developer state.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
*.code-workspace

# ── MSIX / installer / packaging artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The update/delivery channel (ADR 0008) produces these. None of them belongs in git: they are
# large, they are generated, and the signing material must never be tracked at all.
AppPackages/
BundleArtifacts/
*.appx
*.appxbundle
*.appxupload
*.appinstaller
*.msix
*.msixbundle
*.msixupload
*.msi
*.cab
Package.StoreAssociation.xml
_pkginfo.txt
*.pfx
*.p12
*.snk
*.cer
*.publishsettings
PublishProfiles/*.user

# ── Windows / macOS shell debris ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store

# ── Python (tools/coord, tools/doc-audit — stdlib-only, but the interpreter still litters) ───────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# ── Node (the doc/tooling side only; there is no web app in this repository today) ───────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Local, machine-specific, and secret ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rule: if it differs per machine or per person, it is ignored and a committed `*.example` file
# documents its shape. A tracked file must be true on every machine.
*.local
*.local.json
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Local.json
local.settings.json
secrets.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.secrets.*
!*.secrets.example.*
